        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A non-occupational disability is defined as a disability which results from disease, illness or accidental injury, mental or physical incapacity, which is not compensable under the Workers Compensation Act of the State of Michigan. Effective July 1, 1998, this disability can be paid according to the Program Design or the disability can be unpaid.",
